# dbt Secondary Repo Sync

`responsum-team/dbtproject` is the **base repo** — it holds dbt models AND all platform scripts, skills, and rules.
dbt Cloud reads from it directly. Pushing to `elixirrjob1/cursorskills` main is not enough — you must also sync or dbt Cloud will run old code and skills will be out of date.

## What gets synced

| Source (cursorskills) | Destination (dbtproject) |
|---|---|
| `dbt_project/drip_transformations/` | repo root (`dbt_project.yml` must be at root) |
| `scripts/` | `scripts/` |
| `requirements.txt` | `requirements.txt` |
| `.cursor/skills/` | `.cursor/skills/` (test snapshots excluded) |
| `.cursor/rules/` | `.cursor/rules/` |

## When to sync

After any commit that touches dbt models, scripts, skills, rules, or docs.

If you edited platform docs under `docs/`, run `./scripts/sync_onboarding_docs.sh` first so `dbt_project/drip_transformations/docs/` is up to date.

## How to sync (correct method — no force push)

Run the sync script from the repo root. Never force push.

```bash
./scripts/sync_dbt_secondary_repo.sh
```

After syncing, verify `dbt_project.yml` is at root of the secondary repo — if not, dbt Cloud will error with "valid dbt project was not found".

## Common mistakes

- Using `git push --force` to responsum-team/dbtproject — forbidden, always use the sync script above.
- Running `git filter-repo` on the main repo — it removes the `origin` remote and destroys local history.
- Using `scripts/push-dbt-remote.sh` — it attempts a merge pull which causes conflicts. Use the sync script above instead.
- Triggering a dbt Cloud job immediately after pushing to `elixirrjob1/cursorskills` without syncing — the job will run against old code.

## Hash key consistency rule

All FK hashes in fact views must use the same formula as their target dim PK hashes.

DimCustomer and DimProduct PKs are computed as:
```sql
HASH(CAST(id AS VARCHAR) || '|' || 'ERP')
```

FactSales FKs must match:
```sql
HASH(COALESCE(CAST(CUSTOMER_ID AS VARCHAR), '#@#@#@#@#') || '|' || 'ERP') AS "CustomerHashFK"
HASH(COALESCE(CAST(PRODUCT_ID AS VARCHAR), '#@#@#@#@#') || '|' || 'ERP') AS "ProductHashFK"
```

If a FK mismatch is reported, check the hash formula in both the fact view and the dim view before triggering a reload.
